1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,730
Welcome back! Today, we make text slides in the editor.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,740
Open it with Edit on the switch at the bottom left, or the pencil on a title bar.

3
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:21,760
There's no Save button. Whatever you change is saved, however you leave.

4
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:23,420
Press Show to come back.

5
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:30,310
Slides run down the left. New Slide adds one at the end.

6
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:34,990
Across the top is the ribbon, in four rows.

7
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:41,780
Row three is everything about letters. Row four: align, outline, shadow and fit.

8
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:45,420
Hover any button to see its name.

9
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:50,930
Every new slide comes with an empty text box. Double-click it.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,800
Type straight away. Escape ends typing.

11
00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:00,650
The thumbnail on the left follows as you type.

12
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:06,830
Search for a font by any part of its name, then pick a weight.

13
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:14,520
Font size is a percent of the screen's height, so it looks the same in HD and 4K.

14
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:18,660
Drag a number's label to change it. Hold Shift for bigger steps.

15
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:28,620
Now, put a photo behind the words. The Background row imports one, or pastes one you copied.

16
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:33,860
White text over a bright sky almost disappears.

17
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:38,760
Press Outline. The group turns blue, and the words stand out.

18
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:42,480
Text shadow works the same way.

19
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:49,440
The arrow beside it opens distance, angle and blur. A wide blur keeps the shadow soft.

20
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:55,580
White with a black outline reads on a bright sky and a dark stage alike.

21
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:02,650
Drag the box smaller. When the words no longer fit, a small blue plus appears under it.

22
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:08,070
Press it to make the box bigger, or to shrink the text to fit.

23
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:12,340
Look for this badge in rehearsal.

24
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:17,170
Show on output sends the slide you're editing.

25
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,850
While it's on stage, your edits follow, live.

26
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:26,090
Change the text, and the audience sees it at once.

27
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,390
Back in Show, the preview already has it.

28
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:35,610
And the slide is named from its first line.

29
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:41,300
You can now make a text slide that reads over any photo.

30
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:45,390
Next time: designing slides, with shapes, pictures and styles.

